==English==

===Etymology===
Probably representing French ''[[parez]]'', imperative of ''[[parer#French|parer]]'' ‘prepare’.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈpɜɹi/}}
* {{rhymes|æri}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|parries|parrying|parried}}

# To avoid, deflect, or ward off (an attack).

====Translations====
* Finnish: {{t+|fi|torjua}}
* Norwegian: {{t-|no|parere}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|parries}}

# A defensive or deflective action; an act of parrying.
# {{fencing}} A simple defensive action designed to deflect an attack, performed with the [[forte]] of the blade.

